## SECTION 3. CORE CONDITIONS

You may exercise the rights in Section 2 only if You comply with all of the following:

**3.1 HUMAN USE ONLY.** You may use the Licensed Material only for Human Use and other Noncommercial purposes.

**3.2 NO COMMERCIAL USE.** You may not Offer for Value, monetize, sell, resell, sublicense, commercially host, commercially support, commercially integrate, or otherwise use the Licensed Material or any Derivative Work for any commercial purpose. This includes use by a Commercial Entity in furtherance of its commercial activities, regardless of whether the specific use is itself directly monetized.

**3.3 NO GOVERNMENT USE.** You may not provide, license, disclose, deploy, support, train, fine-tune, customize, host, maintain, or otherwise make the Licensed Material or Derivative Works available to any Government Entity, nor use the Licensed Material in performance of any contract, grant, or arrangement with a Government Entity. The academic-research exception in §1.6 narrowly preserves individual researcher access.

**3.4 NO HARMFUL APPLICATION.** You may not use the Licensed Material for any Prohibited Field of Endeavor as enumerated in [`legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md`](legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md).

**3.5 SHAREALIKE; NO ENCLOSURE; SAME LICENSE REQUIRED.** This is the ShareAlike (copyleft) provision. It ensures that all freedoms and prohibitions in this License propagate to every Derivative Work, every downstream redistribution, and every recipient in perpetuity.

If You distribute the Licensed Material or a **Derivative Work**, You must:

(a) provide a copy of this License (and the modular `legal/` layers in current form);
(b) preserve all copyright, attribution, declaration, and notice files including [`legal/CHARTER.md`](legal/CHARTER.md);
(c) clearly mark all modifications, dates of change, and the identity of the modifying party;
(d) license the Derivative Work under **this same License version or a later version published by Licensor**, with no additional restrictions;
(e) **not** impose any further restriction on the recipients' exercise of the rights granted herein;
(f) preserve the trust-held status of the underlying copyright per §15 and [`legal/TRUST_FRAMEWORK.md`](legal/TRUST_FRAMEWORK.md).

**Collective Works** (as defined in §1.10) are distinct: the Licensed Material's License governs the Licensed Material's inclusion; the ShareAlike requirement does not propagate to other independent components of the Collective Work. A standard example: a software distribution including the Licensed Material plus other separately-licensed components is a Collective Work, not a Derivative Work; each component retains its own License.

You may not convert the Licensed Material or any substantial portion of it into proprietary, closed, exclusive, or commercially licensable form. You may not relicense the Licensed Material under any other license.

**Compatibility note.** Material under more permissive ShareAlike licenses (CC BY-SA, GPL, AGPL, SSPL) cannot be relicensed under this License without separate permission from the original copyright holders. Material under this License cannot be relicensed under more permissive ShareAlike licenses. This License is a **one-way valve**.

**3.6 SOURCE AVAILABILITY.** If You distribute object code, binaries, compiled artifacts, hosted instances, model checkpoints, model weights, fine-tuned models, distilled models, embeddings derived from the Licensed Material, or other non-source forms, You must also make the complete corresponding source, training data references, build instructions, training procedure, and reconstruction instructions available to recipients at no charge under this same License, in a form suitable for independent verification and modification.

**3.7 NO TRADEMARK RIGHTS.** This License does not grant any right to use Licensor's names, brands, logos, trademarks, or indicia identifying CK, TIG, 7SiTe, Braiding Fractal, or related marks, except for reasonable attribution per [`legal/NOTICE.md`](legal/NOTICE.md). Full trademark rules in [`legal/TRADEMARKS.md`](legal/TRADEMARKS.md).

**3.8 PRESERVE FREEDOM NOTICES.** You must preserve any notices designated by Licensor as ethical-use, sovereignty, human-freedom, public-benefit, anti-surveillance, anti-enclosure, anti-coercion, or noncommercial notices.

**3.9 NOTICE TO AFFECTED PERSONS.** If Your use processes data of, makes inferences about, or affects any Affected Person, You must, where feasible and lawful, inform those persons of: (a) the use of the Licensed Material in the system affecting them, (b) this License and its restrictions, and (c) means of contacting Licensor regarding misuse.

**3.10 NO CIRCUMVENTION.** You may not use the Licensed Material in a manner designed to circumvent any restriction in this License, including routing prohibited uses through nominally compliant intermediaries; using natural-person fronts for Commercial Entity or Government Entity activity; structuring projects to fragment prohibited use across multiple parties; or using the mathematical claims as backbone for systems whose user-facing form attempts to evade these restrictions.

