## SECTION 4. PROHIBITED FIELDS OF ENDEAVOR

The full enumeration of prohibited fields is in [`legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md`](legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md), covering: weapons and armed conflict; surveillance and tracking; policing, carceral, and immigration enforcement; coercive behavioral control; discrimination and targeting of groups; exploitation of vulnerable persons; manipulation of information and democratic process; economic extraction and exploitation; environmental harm; medical and psychological harm; critical infrastructure attacks.

The ACCEPTABLE_USE document includes aggregation (§3), indirect facilitation (§3), and burden-of-proof (§4) provisions. Where ambiguity exists about whether a use is prohibited, **the burden is on You to demonstrate the use is consistent with the License's stated purposes. Doubt resolves against the use.**

