## SECTION 10. SUCCESSOR ENTITY AND PERPETUITY

**10.1 Designated successor.** Upon the dissolution, insolvency, or permanent ceasing of operations of 7SiTe LLC, all rights, obligations, and authority of the Licensor under this License shall pass to the **Perpetual Purpose Trust** described in [`legal/TRUST_FRAMEWORK.md`](legal/TRUST_FRAMEWORK.md), or to such other successor entity as Licensor has designated **by written agreement of both Licensor and the designated successor** prior to dissolution.

**10.2 Failure of successor designation.** If no successor has been designated by mutual written agreement at the time of Licensor's dissolution, the rights and obligations vest with the public-benefit-non-profit-of-last-resort under the governing jurisdiction's law (probably the Office of the Attorney General of Arkansas, per §14.1).

**10.3 Perpetuity of License terms.** The terms of this License, including all restrictions on commercial, governmental, harmful, and enclosive use, survive in perpetuity. No successor entity has authority to relicense the Licensed Material under more permissive terms, nor to grant exceptions to Section 3, [`legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md`](legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md), or Section 7.

**10.4 Authority to issue later versions.** Licensor (and any successor) may publish later versions of this License, which shall apply only to Licensed Material expressly redistributed under the later version. No later version shall reduce protections afforded by this version with respect to material originally distributed under this version.

