## SECTION 13. SEVERABILITY

If any provision of this License is held unenforceable, that provision shall be reformed only to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, or severed. The remainder of this License (including all modular layers) remains in full force.

The provisions of this License are intended to be severable in a manner that preserves maximum protection. In any case where severability is at issue, the following provisions are preserved with priority, in descending order:

(a) Section 3.2 (No Commercial Use);
(b) Section 3.5 (ShareAlike; No Enclosure);
(c) Section 3.6 (Source Availability);
(d) [`legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md`](legal/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md) with each subsection independently severable;
(e) Section 3.3 (No Government Use), Section 5(b)-(c) (patent grant limits), and Section 7 (Moral Restriction) — each independently severable;
(f) Sections 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 — preserved as administrative provisions.

The unenforceability of [`legal/CHARTER.md`](legal/CHARTER.md) or any other binding-as-instruction layer shall not be deemed to invalidate the operative copyright + contract grant in this License.

